                      "id": "shelfkit-stack",
                      "tags": ["cloudflare", "rust", "typescript"],
                      "title": "TypeScript on Cloudflare Workers with Rust core",
                      "conventions": [
                        {
                          "body": "moon orchestrates tasks and proto pins every toolchain from .prototools. Do not add a task moon does not know about.",
                          "heading": "Repository"
                        },
                        {
                          "body": "The shelf format, validation, revision hashing, and profile resolution live in Rust under crates/. They compile native for the CLI and to WASM for the Worker, so the browser preview and the CLI cannot disagree.",
                          "heading": "Core logic"
                        },
                        {
                          "body": "One Durable Object per shelf with its own SQLite database, accessed through drizzle-orm/durable-sqlite. There is no D1 database and no cross-shelf query. Content lives in R2 keyed by sha256.",
                          "heading": "Storage"
                        },
                        {
                          "body": "APM owns install, resolution, and the lockfile. ShelfKit writes apm.yml and stops. Never parse human-oriented apm output: only audit, deps why, pack, policy status, targets, and lock export emit structured data.",
                          "heading": "APM"
                        },
                        {
                          "body": "Use APM's target slugs verbatim. Emit only the OpenAPM v0.1 canonical producer set by default; anything outside it is an explicit opt-in that check must report.",
                          "heading": "Targets"
                        }
                      ],
